title: Tackle Context Usage Visibility Tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-10-20
author: adrian
items[10]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,[x] Pricing lookup,"Add `request_cost(model_ref, input_tokens, output_tokens) -> Option<f64>` to `agent/config_options.rs`. Split the endpoint-qualified model reference, look up `providers[endpoint].models[model]` in `bundled_snapshot_parsed`, and sum the input and output per-million-token rates. Return `None` when the provider or model is absent or neither rate exists; treat an explicit zero rate as known.","Unit tests cover a priced provider/model, an unknown endpoint, a model missing from a known provider, input-only pricing, output-only pricing, and an explicit zero rate; `cargo test -p agentkit-tackle config_options` passes",low,"1-2h",,"cumulative-cost,cost-omission"
  T-002,[x] Optional cost through the sink,"Change `TurnSink::usage` to take `Option<f64>`. Add a shared `usage_update(used, size, cost)` constructor in `acp_v1/sink.rs` that attaches `Cost::new(amount, \"USD\")` only for `Some`. Update `ConnectionTurnSink` and the context-overflow fallback to use it so omitted cost means unchanged.","The crate compiles with the new signature; a sink unit test asserts that `Some` produces a cost-bearing update and `None` omits the field; the overflow fallback still emits a usage update",low,"1-2h","T-001","usage-update-contract,cumulative-cost,cost-omission"
  T-003,[x] Turn and session cost accumulation,"In `agent/turn.rs`, track whether any request in the turn was priced. On each response add `request_cost` to `TurnUsage.cost_usd`, persist the delta, read `session_usage`, and pass `Some(cumulative)` when any cost is known, including a prior turn's cost, or `None` otherwise. Keep request-cap, tool-loop, and stop-reason paths unchanged.","A stub-provider turn with a priced model persists the expected per-turn cost and emits a usage update carrying the cumulative session cost; a turn with an unpriced model emits no cost; multi-request turns sum their requests without double counting",medium,"2-3h","T-001,T-002","cumulative-cost,cost-omission,usage-update-contract"
  T-004,[x] Lifecycle usage snapshots,"Add `send_usage_snapshot` in `acp_v1/sessions.rs`: resolve the effective model, return early when the window is unknown, estimate `used` from assembled content, read cumulative cost, and send exactly one update. Call it after the `session/new` response and command advertisement, after the `session/resume` response and notices, and after the `session/load` response while replay stays before the response. Leave `session/fork` unchanged.","Integration tests count exactly one usage update after new, resume, and load; load replay still precedes the response; each snapshot carries the effective window and cumulative cost when known; unknown-window models emit none",medium,"2-4h","T-002,T-003","lifecycle-snapshots,usage-update-contract"
  T-005,[x] Compaction usage cost,"Update the post-compaction `usage_update` in `acp_v1/prompt.rs` to read cumulative session usage and pass it through the shared constructor. Leave the announcement text and the RFD-shaped compaction update untouched.","A compaction integration test observes a usage update with the same used/size as today and a cumulative cost when pricing is known; clients without unstable compaction support see no change",low,"1-2h","T-002,T-003","cumulative-cost,cost-omission"
  T-006,[x] Tagged prior messages and shared system builder,"Make `build_registry_and_system` in `agent/prompt.rs` `pub(crate)`. Add `compaction::prior_messages_tagged` returning each assembled message with its turn kind, and keep `prior_messages` as a thin adapter for the turn loop. The tagged path must apply the same role filtering, empty-content filtering, and summary wrapping as today.","Unit tests assert that a compaction summary is tagged as a summary and remains wrapped, tool messages are still filtered, and the model turn's prior messages are byte-identical to the current output",medium,"1-2h",,"estimation-basis"
  T-007,Context report builder,"Add `agent/context_report.rs` with a report struct and renderer. Inputs: system prompt, tool definitions, tagged prior messages, window size, and session usage. Count system and serialized tool-catalogue bytes, then per-category text and image payload bytes, convert through `estimate_tokens`, compute percentage and free space only when the window is known, and format the fixed ASCII layout with comma grouping and the exact column widths.","Golden-text tests cover a known window and cost, an unknown window with `-` shares and no Free row, unknown cost with the footer ending after output, zero categories, an over-window estimate, and image payload accounting; the renderer uses no ANSI, markdown, or emoji",medium,"3-4h","T-006","composition-report,estimation-basis,unknown-window"
  T-008,Context command advertisement,"Add `builtins/context-prompt.md` with the description `Show estimated context-window composition and session usage`, no parameters, and a body that is never expanded. Register it as `CONTEXT_PROMPT` in `builtins/assets.rs` and in `defaults()`.","The existing available-commands integration test sees `context` after session/new and session/load; the command has no input hint; the built-in definition loads without a trust prompt",low,"1h",,"context-command"
  T-009,Ephemeral context handler and dispatch,"Add `acp_v1/context.rs` with `run_context_case`: fetch the session, resolve the actor, build the runtime, build the system prompt and tools, assemble context, render the report, stream one `agent_message_chunk` with a generated id, delete the command turn, release the lease, and respond `end_turn`. Wire exact `/context` dispatch in `acp_v1/server.rs` after actor resolution and before compaction. On any error delete the turn and release the lease before returning the precise no-model or internal error.","An integration test sends `/context` and receives the report with no model request and no tool card; the prompt turn is deleted and the session head is unchanged; a later turn's assembled context and a session/load replay contain neither the command nor the report; the no-model path returns the specified error after cleanup",high,"3-4h","T-007,T-008","context-command,ephemeral-reply,composition-report"
  T-010,End-to-end usage and context coverage,"Extend the existing ACP integration harness with lifecycle and command coverage: cost-bearing updates for a priced endpoint, cost omission for an unpriced endpoint, exactly one snapshot per lifecycle path, unknown-window behaviour, and the ephemeral `/context` round-trip. Reuse the stub provider and in-process client rather than adding a new harness.","The new tests run offline in CI; they assert cost presence and omission, snapshot counts and ordering, unknown-window silence, `/context` output, turn deletion, and no replay; the full `cargo test -p agentkit-tackle` suite passes",medium,"2-3h","T-004,T-005,T-009","testability,usage-update-contract,cost-omission,context-report,context-ephemeral"
